# StillFlow Engineering

Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/data-ingestion-architecture.md` before changing backend code.

## Hard rules

- `stillflow-core`: domain types, errors, events, `RequestContext`, `BatchStream` only. No Polars/DuckDB/SQLx/Axum.
- Use `arrow-array` + `arrow-schema`; never the `arrow` meta crate.
- `stillflow-connectors`: trait + capabilities + registry only. Adapters go in separate modules/crates.
- Dependency direction: `api → engine → connectors → core`.
- Unsupported optimizations return `ConnectorError` with `UnsupportedCapability` — never silent fallback.
- Secrets via `CredentialRef` only; run `ensure_no_secret_fields` on connection config.
- Do not modify `SourceConnector` or core public types unless the active Implementation Contract allows it.

## Implementation discipline

- One GitHub Issue per branch (`agent/issue-NNN-*`).
- Do not touch `main` directly.
- Do not modify frontend layout/CSS unless explicitly requested.
- Prefer focused diffs; no drive-by refactors.
- Report contract deviations, new deps, and `unwrap`/`expect` in the completion summary.

## Tests required before handoff

```bash
cd backend
cargo fmt --all -- --check
cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo test --workspace
```

## Stop and escalate

Stop if you need to change frozen connector contracts. File a contract revision request to Sol instead of redefining traits in an adapter PR.
